window.docContents[129].resolve({"/Basic-Types/Strings/#Lean-__________________--Basic-Types--Strings--Logical-Model--Backwards-Compatibility":{"contents":"In prior versions of Lean, the logical model of strings was a structure that contained a list of characters.\nThis model is still useful.\nIt is still accessible using String.ofList, which converts a list of characters into a String, and String.toList, which converts a String into a list of characters.\n\nCreates a string that contains the characters in a list, in order.Examples:* String.ofList ['L', '∃', '∀', 'N'] = \"L∃∀N\"* String.ofList [] = \"\"* String.ofList ['a', 'a', 'a'] = \"aaa\"\n\nConverts a string to a list of characters.Since strings are represented as dynamic arrays of bytes containing the string encoded using\nUTF-8, this operation takes time and space linear in the length of the string.Examples:* \"abc\".toList = ['a', 'b', 'c']* \"\".toList = []* \"\\n\".toList = ['\\n']\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009Basic Types\u0009Strings\u0009Logical Model","header":"20.8.1.1. Backwards Compatibility","id":"/Basic-Types/Strings/#Lean-__________________--Basic-Types--Strings--Logical-Model--Backwards-Compatibility"},"/Basic-Types/The-Unit-Type/#Lean-__________________--Basic-Types--The-Unit-Type":{"contents":"The unit type is the canonical type with exactly one element, named unit and represented by the empty tuple ().\nIt describes only a single value, which consists of said constructor applied to no arguments whatsoever.\n\nUnit is analogous to void in languages derived from C: even though void has no elements that can be named, it represents the return of control flow from a function with no additional information.\nIn functional programming, Unit is the return type of things that “return nothing”.\nMathematically, this is represented by a single completely uninformative value, as opposed to an empty type such as Empty, which represents unreachable code.\n\nWhen programming with monads, Unit is especially useful.\nFor any type α, m α represents an action that has side effects and returns a value of type α.\nThe type m Unit represents an action that has some side effects but does not return a value.\n\nThere are two variants of the unit type:\n\n* Unit is a Type that exists in the smallest non-propositional universe.* PUnit is universe polymorphic and can be used in any non-propositional universe.\n\nBehind the scenes, Unit is actually defined as PUnit.{1}.\nUnit should be preferred over PUnit when possible to avoid unnecessary universe parameters.\nIf in doubt, use Unit until universe errors occur.\n\nThe canonical type with one element. This element is written ().Unit has a number of uses:* It can be used to model control flow that returns from a function call without providing other\ninformation.* Monadic actions that return Unit have side effects without computing values.* In polymorphic types, it can be used to indicate that no data is to be stored in a particular\nfield.\n\nThe only element of the unit type.It can be written as an empty tuple: ().\n\nThe canonical universe-polymorphic type with just one element.It should be used in contexts that require a type to be universe polymorphic, thus disallowing\nUnit.The only element of the universe-polymorphic unit type.\n\n\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009Basic Types","header":"20.9. The Unit Type","id":"/Basic-Types/The-Unit-Type/#Lean-__________________--Basic-Types--The-Unit-Type"},"/Build-Tools-and-Distribution/Lake/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Build-Tools-and-Distribution--Lake--Command-Line-Interface--Options":{"contents":"Lake 的命令行界面提供了许多全局选项以及执行重要任务的子命令。\n单字符标志不能组合；-HR 不等于 -H -R。\n\n --version\n\nLake 输出其版本并退出，不执行任何其他操作。\n\n --help 或 -h\n\nLake 输出其版本以及使用信息并退出，不执行任何其他操作。\n  子命令可以与 --help 一起使用，在这种情况下将输出该子命令的使用信息。\n\n --dir 或 -d\n\n将提供的目录而不是当前工作目录用作包的位置。\n  这并不总是等同于先更改到该目录，因为会使用当前目录的工具链文件指示的 lake 版本，而不是 DIR 的版本。\n\n --file 或 -f\n\n使用指定的包配置文件而不是默认文件。\n\n --old\n\n仅重新构建修改的模块，忽略传递依赖项。\n  导入修改模块的模块将不会被重新构建。\n  为了实现这一点，将使用文件修改时间而不是哈希来确定模块是否已更改。\n\n --rehash 或 -H\n\n忽略缓存的文件哈希，重新计算它们。\n  Lake 使用依赖项的哈希来确定是否重新构建工件。\n  每当构建模块时，这些哈希都会缓存在磁盘上。\n  为了在构建过程中节省时间，除非指定了 --rehash，否则会使用这些缓存的哈希，而不是重新计算每个哈希。\n\n --allow-empty\n\n接受在未配置默认目标时产生无输出的构建。\n\n --update\n\n在加载包配置之后、但在执行其他任务（例如构建）之前更新依赖项。\n  这等同于在选定命令之前运行 lake update，但由于不需要加载配置两次，它可能会更快。\n\n --packages\n\n使用指定的包覆盖文件。\n  可以多次指定此选项以添加更多覆盖（后指定的覆盖优先）。\n  包覆盖的完整集合还将包括来自 .lake/package-overrides.json 的覆盖（如果有）。\n  但是，通过此选项提供的覆盖具有更高的优先级。\n\n  --reconfigure 或 -R\n\n通常，包配置文件在首次配置包时由精译器处理，并将结果缓存到供将来调用使用的 .olean 文件中，直到包配置发生更改。\n  提供此标志将导致配置文件被重新精译。\n\n --keep-toolchain\n\n默认情况下，Lake 会尝试更新本地工作区的工具链文件。\n  提供此标志会禁用自动更新工具链。\n\n --no-build\n\n如果构建目标不是最新的，Lake 会立即退出，并返回非零的退出代码。\n\n --no-cache\n\n不使用可用的云构建缓存，而是在本地构建所有包。\n  构建缓存不被下载。\n\n --try-cache\n\n尝试下载支持的包的构建缓存\n\n\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009构建工具\u0009Lake\u0009命令行界面","header":"24.1.2.2. 选项","id":"/Build-Tools-and-Distribution/Lake/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Build-Tools-and-Distribution--Lake--Command-Line-Interface--Options"},"/Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation/Varieties-of-Monads/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation--Varieties-of-Monads--Combined-Error-and-State-Monads--Implementations":{"contents":"通常不会直接调用这些函数，而是通过相应的类型类访问它们。\n\n使用函数变换 EStateM ε σ 动作返回的值。\n\n返回一个值，而不修改状态或抛出异常。\n\n依次执行两个 EStateM ε σ 动作，将第一个动作返回的值传给第二个动作。\n\n不依赖具体异常值的失败处理。Backtrackable δ σ 实例用于在运行 x₁ 之前保存部分状态的快照。如果捕获到异常，则使用保存的快照更新状态，从而回滚部分状态。如果没有提供 Backtrackable 实例，则使用 δ 为 Unit 的后备实例，不回滚任何信息。\n\n另一种 orElse 运算符，允许调用者在两个操作都失败时选择应使用哪个异常。默认使用第一个异常，因为标准的 orElse 使用第二个。\n\n依次执行两个 EStateM ε σ 动作，先运行 x，再运行 y。忽略第一个动作的返回值。\n\n处理状态与错误组合单子中抛出的异常。Backtrackable δ σ 实例用于在运行 x 之前保存部分状态的快照。如果捕获到异常，则使用保存的快照更新状态，从而回滚部分状态。如果没有提供 Backtrackable 实例，则使用 δ 为 Unit 的后备实例，不回滚任何信息。\n\n向最近的外围处理器抛出类型为 ε 的异常。\n\n取得单子可变状态的当前值。\n\n用新值替换单子的可变状态的当前值。\n\n对当前状态应用一个函数，该函数既计算新状态也计算一个值。新状态替换当前状态，并返回该值。它等价于 do let (a, s) := f (← get); set s; pure a。但是，使用 modifyGet 可能具有更高的性能，因为它不会增加对状态值的新引用。额外的引用会妨碍数据的原地更新。\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009函子、单子与  do  记法\u0009单子的种类\u0009组合错误与状态单子","header":"18.5.8.2. 实现","id":"/Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation/Varieties-of-Monads/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation--Varieties-of-Monads--Combined-Error-and-State-Monads--Implementations"},"/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/#tactic-language-assumptions":{"contents":"许多策略提供了为其引入的假设指定名称的方法。\nintro 和 intros 例如会接受假设名称作为参数；induction 的 with 形式则可以同时选择分支、命名假设并聚焦。\n假设没有名称时，可以使用 next、case 或 rename_i 为其分配名称。\n\nrename_i x_1 ... x_n renames the last n inaccessible names using the given names.\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009策略证明\u0009策略语言\u0009名称与卫生性","header":"14.3.2.1. 访问假设","id":"/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/#tactic-language-assumptions"},"/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/#tactic-language-unfolding":{"contents":"默认情况下，除检查定义相等性时外，只有标记为可归约的定义才会展开。\n这些运算符可以在策略脚本的某一部分调整此默认行为。\n\nwith_reducible_and_instances tacs executes tacs using the .instances transparency setting.\nIn this setting only definitions tagged as [reducible] or type class instances are unfolded.\n\nwith_reducible tacs executes tacs using the reducible transparency setting.\nIn this setting only definitions tagged as [reducible] are unfolded.\n\nwith_unfolding_all tacs executes tacs using the .all transparency setting.\nIn this setting all definitions that are not opaque are unfolded.\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009策略证明\u0009策略语言\u0009命名空间与选项管理","header":"14.3.6.1. 控制展开","id":"/Tactic-Proofs/The-Tactic-Language/#tactic-language-unfolding"},"/releases/v4.24.0/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Release-Notes--Lean-4___24___0-_LPAR_2025-10-14_RPAR_--Documentation":{"contents":"* #9956 为 let 与 have 策略的文档字符串补充了更多信息，包括不透明性、各自适用时机以及相关策略。\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009发行说明\u0009Lean 4.24.0 (2025-10-14)","header":"文档","id":"/releases/v4.24.0/#The-Lean-Language-Reference--Release-Notes--Lean-4___24___0-_LPAR_2025-10-14_RPAR_--Documentation"}});